{
  "generated_description": "Crime in India compiles long-running, edition-wise statistics on cognizable crimes and related criminal justice indicators for India from 1953 to 2023. It covers major crime categories under IPC and local/special laws, including offences such as murder, kidnapping and abduction, rape, theft/robbery, and dacoity, along with victim profiles and outcomes like disposal of cases and trial-related information. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs and the National Crime Records Bureau (NCRB), the series supports trend analysis, policy monitoring, and research on policing and criminal justice performance.",
  "generated_sector": "Home Affairs and Enforcement; Police"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides Census 2001 statistics on institutional households, broken down by household size, for India and its States. It supports analysis of housing and household composition in institutional settings and can be used for demographic research, planning, and comparative studies across administrative regions. The data are published by the Ministry of Home Affairs, Department of Home, and the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India, under a central government framework.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Motor Transport Statistics compiles time-series information on road transport in India from 1970-71 to 2001-2002 across multiple editions. It covers key indicators such as registered motor vehicles, road accidents (persons killed and injured), national highway length, and the physical and financial performance of State Road Transport Undertakings (SRTUs), including revenue and outlay. The series also tracks licensing activity for drivers and conductors. Published by the Ministry of Road Transport and Highways, it supports monitoring, policy analysis, and trend studies in road transport and safety.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Road Transport"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog presents Census-based counts of non-workers by main activity, age and sex for India and its States/UTs, covering categories such as students, household duties, dependents, retired persons/pensioners, beggars, vagrants and rentiers. It supports demographic and labour-force analysis by showing how non-working populations vary across age groups and between males and females. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs and the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India, the data spans the 1991, 2001 and 2011 Census editions.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides state/UT-wise counts of newly registered motor vehicles and the total number of registered motor vehicles, with vehicles grouped into Transport and Non-Transport categories. It supports analysis of mobility trends, growth in vehicle ownership, and planning for road transport infrastructure and regulatory needs. Published by the Ministry of Road Transport and Highways, the coverage spans 35 States/UTs across the merged scope. Temporal coverage is not specified in the provided metadata.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Road Transport"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog supports solid waste management planning and operations for the City of Chennai, Tamil Nadu. It covers household-level source segregation, door-to-door (D2D) collection efficiency, bin placement and sizing, and details on collection vehicles and their capacities. It also describes waste processing pathways and disposal options for collected waste, enabling better sanitation and service delivery. Published under the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs through the Smart Cities Mission, with involvement of Tamil Nadu and Chennai.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Municipal Waste, Water and Sanitation; Sanitation"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Union Budget datasets provide fiscal estimates and accounts for India’s central government, covering receipts and expenditures, including revenue and capital components, taxes, subsidies, and deficit indicators. Published as the Annual Financial Statement under Article 112 of the Constitution, the catalog supports analysis of budget allocations, revised estimates, and expenditure planning across key budget heads. It spans the Union Budget editions 2018-19, 2021-22, 2022-23, and 2023-24, and is maintained by the Ministry of Finance, Department of Economic Affairs.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Union Budget 2019-20 (Interim) presents the Government of India’s interim annual financial statement, covering key budget aggregates such as receipts, expenditure and deficit. It supports analysis of fiscal performance and helps stakeholders compare revenue and spending priorities for the central government during 2019-20. Published by the Ministry of Finance, Department of Economic Affairs, the budget information is provided for India at national coverage and is useful for policy review, budgeting, and economic research.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Village/Town-wise Primary Census Abstract provides 2011 Census statistics for households and population at the village and town level across 34 States/UTs. It covers key demographic indicators such as age-group 0–6 population, SC/ST population, literacy and illiteracy, and workforce participation including main and marginal workers with broad worker categories. The data supports research and planning for governance, education, labour and livelihoods, and targeted social development. Published by the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India under the Ministry of Home Affairs.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}
